---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';

type Extrema = { minimum: number; maximum: number };
type Group = {
	dimension: string;
	group: string;
	modeled_2024_county_participants: number;
	modeled_2026_participants: number;
	modeled_cohort_counts: Record<string, number>;
	modeled_prior_choice_transitions: Record<string, Record<string, number>>;
	margin_pp_contributions: Record<string, number>;
};
type GroupRange = {
	dimension: string;
	group: string;
	modeled_2024_county_participants: Extrema;
	modeled_2026_participants: Extrema;
	modeled_cohort_counts: Record<string, Extrema>;
	modeled_prior_choice_transitions: Record<string, Record<string, Extrema>>;
	margin_pp_contributions: Record<string, Extrema>;
};
type Analysis = {
	default_conditional_scenario: { swing_margin_pp: number; demographics: Group[]; margin_pp_contributions: Record<string, number> };
	demographic_sensitivity_range_margin_pp: GroupRange[];
	sensitivity_range_margin_pp: Record<string, Extrema>;
};
const base = '/participation-county-scenarios/20261107-01/';
const analysis: Analysis = JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}summary.json`, 'utf8'));
const reference = analysis.default_conditional_scenario;
const dimensions = [
	['overall', 'Whole county'], ['age_2024', 'Age in 2024'], ['race', 'Administrative race'],
	['ethnicity', 'Administrative Hispanic ethnicity'], ['administrative_gender', 'Administrative gender'],
];
const activities = [
	['modeled_2024_county_participants', '2024 participants'],
	['modeled_2026_participants', '2026 participants'],
	['repeat_2024_county_participants', 'Repeat participants'],
	['prior_county_participants_now_nonvoting', 'Modeled nonvoting'],
	['prior_county_participants_eligibility_residence_exit', 'Modeled exit'],
	['participants_without_2024_county_participation', 'Without 2024 county participation'],
	['republican_to_democratic', 'Trump → D'],
	['democratic_to_republican', 'Harris → R'],
];
const components = [
	['switching', 'Switching'], ['dropoff', 'Participation drop-off'],
	['new_returning', 'Previously eligible new / returning'],
	['eligibility_residence', 'Eligibility / residence change'], ['other_and_contest', 'Other / contest effects'],
];
const flows = ['original_2024_county_presidential_voters', 'D', 'R', 'O', 'B', 'N', 'X'];
const count = (value: number) => (Math.round(value / 100) * 100).toLocaleString('en-US');
const points = (value: number) => `${value >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${value.toFixed(2)}`;
const counts = (group: Group): Record<string, number> => ({
	...group.modeled_cohort_counts, modeled_2024_county_participants: group.modeled_2024_county_participants,
	modeled_2026_participants: group.modeled_2026_participants,
});
const range = (group: Group): GroupRange => analysis.demographic_sensitivity_range_margin_pp.find(
	row => row.dimension === group.dimension && row.group === group.group)!;
const countRanges = (group: Group): Record<string, Extrema> => ({
	...range(group).modeled_cohort_counts,
	modeled_2024_county_participants: range(group).modeled_2024_county_participants,
	modeled_2026_participants: range(group).modeled_2026_participants,
});
const labels: Record<string, string> = {
	'All groups': 'Whole county', ASIAN: 'Asian', 'BLACK or AFRICAN AMERICAN': 'Black or African American',
	WHITE: 'White', 'HISPANIC or LATINO': 'Hispanic or Latino',
	'NOT HISPANIC or NOT LATINO': 'Not Hispanic or Latino', FEMALE: 'Female', MALE: 'Male',
};
---

<section id="participation-county-scenarios" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="county-scenarios-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">Experimental county model · 2024 President → 2026 Senate</p>
		<h2 id="county-scenarios-title">Wake County: participation and switching, separately estimated</h2>
		<p>The observed two-party margin moved <strong>{points(reference.swing_margin_pp)} points toward Democrats</strong>.
			The model separates switching, nonvoting, entry and exit, while matching the county’s
			candidate and ballot totals. These are <strong>conditional scenarios, not observed individual persuasion</strong>.</p>
	</header>
	<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Wake conditional swing contributions">
		<table>
			<caption>Signed contributions to two-party margin change, in percentage points.
				All 86 tested assumptions; sensitivity ranges are not confidence intervals and endpoints are not additive.</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">Component</th><th scope="col">Reference</th><th scope="col">Tested range</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>{components.map(([key, label]) => <tr data-county-component={key}>
				<th scope="row">{label}</th><td>{points(reference.margin_pp_contributions[key])}</td>
				<td>{points(analysis.sensitivity_range_margin_pp[key].minimum)} to {points(analysis.sensitivity_range_margin_pp[key].maximum)}</td>
			</tr>)}</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p><strong>Material calibration limits:</strong> retrospective 2022 turnout error was +9.74 percentage points.
		Even after matching the known 2022 total, subgroup errors reached 8.84 points for groups of at least 100.
		Matching totals verifies constraints, <strong>not individual transitions or demographic accuracy</strong>.</p>
	<p>The frozen, provisional 2026 snapshot reports <strong>525,061 ballots and 216 of 216 reporting units</strong>
		at November 3, 11:56 p.m., retrieved November 4. The 2024 history contains 656,871 county participants.
		These are not final 2026 totals or proof of a counted fixed early-voter cohort.</p>
	<p>Below, model counts are rounded to the nearest 100; smaller text gives the range across all 86 scenarios.
		“Nonvoting” is modeled separately from assumed eligibility/residence exit.
		<strong>Measured staying home and demographic eligible-population turnout rates are unavailable.</strong></p>

	{dimensions.map(([dimension, title]) => <details class="explorer-notes" data-county-dimension={dimension}>
		<summary>{title}: participation, prior-choice transitions and swing contributions</summary>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`Wake ${title} modeled participation`}>
			<table>
				<caption>{title}. Reference counts and assumption ranges, not independently observed demographic outcomes.
					Selected rows are not exhaustive partitions; withheld groups are not zero.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">Source-defined group</th>{activities.map(([, label]) => <th scope="col">{label}</th>)}</tr></thead>
				<tbody>{reference.demographics.filter(group => group.dimension === dimension).map(group =>
					<tr data-county-group={group.group} data-county-kind="activity">
						<th scope="row" title={group.group}>{labels[group.group] || group.group}</th>
						{activities.map(([key]) => <td data-county-count={key} data-value={counts(group)[key]}>
							{count(counts(group)[key])}<small>{count(countRanges(group)[key].minimum)}–{count(countRanges(group)[key].maximum)}</small>
						</td>)}
					</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`Wake ${title} modeled prior-choice destinations`}>
			<table>
				<caption>Within modeled prior Harris / Trump coalitions: all six 2026 destinations, not just returning voters.
					D/R = Senate choice; O = other; B = ballot without selected-contest vote;
					N = modeled nonvoting; X = modeled eligibility/residence exit. Original group choice is modeled.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">Source-defined group</th><th scope="col">Modeled 2024 choice</th>
					<th scope="col">Original coalition</th>{['D', 'R', 'O', 'B', 'N', 'X'].map(key => <th scope="col">{key}</th>)}</tr></thead>
				<tbody>{reference.demographics.filter(group => group.dimension === dimension).flatMap(group =>
					['D', 'R'].map(prior => <tr data-county-group={group.group} data-county-prior={prior}>
						<th scope="row" title={group.group}>{labels[group.group] || group.group}</th>
						<td>{prior === 'D' ? 'Harris' : 'Trump'}</td>
						{flows.map(key => <td data-county-flow={key} data-value={group.modeled_prior_choice_transitions[prior][key]}>
							{count(group.modeled_prior_choice_transitions[prior][key])}
							<small>{count(range(group).modeled_prior_choice_transitions[prior][key].minimum)}–{count(range(group).modeled_prior_choice_transitions[prior][key].maximum)}</small>
						</td>)}
					</tr>))}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`Wake ${title} modeled swing contributions`}>
			<table>
				<caption>Signed contribution to whole-county margin change, not the group’s own swing or a causal persuasion effect.
					Values are percentage points; ranges are marginal, nonadditive sensitivity.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">Source-defined group</th>{components.map(([, label]) => <th scope="col">{label}</th>)}</tr></thead>
				<tbody>{reference.demographics.filter(group => group.dimension === dimension).map(group =>
					<tr data-county-group={group.group} data-county-kind="contribution">
						<th scope="row" title={group.group}>{labels[group.group] || group.group}</th>
						{components.map(([key]) => <td data-county-contribution={key}>
							{points(group.margin_pp_contributions[key])}
							<small>{points(range(group).margin_pp_contributions[key].minimum)} to {points(range(group).margin_pp_contributions[key].maximum)}</small>
						</td>)}
					</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>)}

	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Scope, missing populations, entrant definitions and complete reproduction</summary>
		<p>Age is measured in 2024; race, ethnicity and gender use current administrative attributes, not fixed observed
			historical cohorts. Race and Hispanic ethnicity are separate, overlapping dimensions. Education and income
			are not supplied. Do not sum dimensions, infer omitted categories, or allocate county results to precincts or other states.</p>
		<p>The private linkage retains 24,904 prior participants without current registration. Missing or removed records
			do not prove death, migration or ineligibility; exit fractions are assumed and varied. Unknown populations
			remain in the whole-county accounting, not silently deleted. Several race categories are withheld together
			so that a small category cannot be recovered by subtracting all other categories from the total.</p>
		<p>“Without 2024 county participation” includes positive 2024 history elsewhere in North Carolina,
			newly adult entrants and people without a North Carolina match whose national history remains unresolved.
			The archive retains these three categories separately for every selected group and scenario.
			Neither a new registration nor a missing history match proves first-ever voting.</p>
		<p>Accepted early/mail membership is not counted contest membership; absence from that cohort is not Election Day
			nonparticipation. Current-registration survivor selection, changing residence/attributes, mortality,
			history coverage, choice-model error and distinct source clocks remain unresolved.
			The county-specific comparison is President to Senate, not a pooled House or causal campaign effect.</p>
		<p>The complete download includes every selected broad result for all 86 scenarios, full public candidate/ballot
			inputs, fitted historical coefficients, source receipts, model/linkage code, tests and qualifications.
			Offline reproduction regenerates the selected summary and archive.
			<strong>A fresh latent fit needs excluded private records and fine joint cells.</strong>
			Public reproduction is not an independent refit or verification of individual switching.</p>
		<p>Sources: North Carolina State Board of Elections and CES 2024 release 9, DOI 10.7910/DVN/X11EP6 (CC0).
			Analysis is not endorsed by the data providers. Existing Durham and survey releases are unchanged;
			Wake is an additional pilot, not completed nationwide or precinct coverage.</p>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${base}complete-analysis.zip`} download>Complete Wake scenarios + permitted inputs + code + results (ZIP)</a>
		<a href={`${base}summary.json`} download>Wake reference, ranges + qualifications (JSON)</a>
		<a href={`${base}download.json`} download>Wake archive bytes and SHA-256</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-county-scenarios { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
	#participation-county-scenarios small { display: block; color: var(--color-text-muted, #666); font-size: .78rem; }
	#participation-county-scenarios .table-wrap { max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; }
	#participation-county-scenarios td { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
</style>
